<title>CANADA: Canada October housing starts fall 9.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada October housing starts fall 9.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian housing starts fell by 9.8 percent in October to a seasonally adjusted annual rate (SAAR) of 118,100 units from a revised 130,900 units in September, the Canada Mortgage and Housing Corp (CMHC) said on Friday.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of economists had forecast housing starts of 135,300 units.</p>
<p>Actual housing starts fell to 10,530 in October from 12,158 the month before. The SAAR is a monthly figure adjusted to remove normal seasonal variation and multiplied by 12.</p>
</text>
